{ % vim: set ft=djot : % }

# Contributing to djotls

## Commit messages

For LLM-assisted changes, include the following trailer in the commit
message, following the Linux kernel contribution policy:

``` text
Assisted-by: LLM
```

## Editing conventions

Use standard Rust formatting and preserve existing SPDX headers. Update
user-facing guides when behavior changes. Keep design reasons beside the
relevant code, linking longer investigations when needed.

## Code map

The main entry points are `src/parser/` for parsing, `src/fmt.rs` for
formatting, `src/analysis/` for document analysis and `src/lsp.rs` for
the language server protocol adapter.

See the [README](README.dj) for build and usage commands and the [LSP
guide](docs/lsp.dj) for supported behavior and workspace limitations.

## Tests

Initialize the reference submodules and run the full suite before
submitting changes:

``` bash
git submodule update --init --recursive
DJOTLS_REQUIRE_CONFORMANCE=1 cargo test --release
cargo fmt --check
cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
```

Parser conformance tests require Node.js and npm; the harness builds the
reference CLI and installs its locked dependencies when needed. Set
`DJOTLS_REQUIRE_CONFORMANCE=1` to prevent missing prerequisites from
silently skipping conformance tests. Documentation and workspace
protocol
tests require Git on `PATH`.

Add regression tests for behavior changes. Formatter fixtures pair
`tests/<name>.in` with `tests/<name>.out`; every `.out` is also checked
for idempotency. Add `{ % @columns: N % }` to an input to set its test
width (default 72).

Opt-in memory probes are described in [memory measurement](
docs/memory.dj).

## Documentation

Maintain project guides in `.dj` format. Keep `AGENTS.md` in Markdown
and CLI help in `docs/long_about.txt` and `docs/after_help.txt` as plain
text. Submodule documentation and license texts retain their upstream
formats.

Declare project Djot document copyright and licensing in `REUSE.toml`,
since REUSE does not recognize Djot comment delimiters.

All project `.dj` documents are automatically checked for formatter
idempotency and parser conformance, including new, non-ignored files.
Third-party submodules and ignored files are excluded. Format changed
documents before running
tests, for example:

``` bash
cargo run -r -- -i README.dj CONTRIBUTING.dj docs/*.dj
```

## Debugging

Use `-vv` to log parser events and source text, or `-vvv` to include
formatter state and file operations:

``` bash
cargo run -- -vvv input.dj
```
